<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Cervera–Levin–Mafe gap-junction reaction–diffusion and bioelectric synthesis faithfully reproduces Planarians; photograph is Schmidtea mediterranea, empirical PlanformDB subset is Dugesia japonica morphology" ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py, 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Planarians; photograph is Schmidtea mediterranea, empirical PlanformDB subset is Dugesia japonica specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 44.9/100, audit 2026-10-17-cervera-audit) and the assessments." ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e71ca55/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e71ca55/2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py; output: cervera_levin_mafe_gj_block.gif; organism: Planarians; photograph is Schmidtea mediterranea, empirical PlanformDB subset is Dugesia japonica; checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/e71ca55; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0, scipy 1.16.3, scikit-image 0.26.0; other sources: Smediterranea.jpg, from A Low Percent Ethanol Method for Immobilizing Planarians <https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Smediterranea.jpg>, MesmerPrism/rusty-matter planarian bioelectric circuit and fixtures <https://github.com/MesmerPrism/rusty-matter/tree/ad111fa7ecfd8f43d292ff3b1d27d3af2741d828>" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bioelechem.2019.107410>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.biosystems.2021.104511>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bpj.2019.01.029>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ydbio.2009.12.012>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1093/bioinformatics/btt088> ;
    pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-cervera-levin-mafe-code-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-cervera-levin-mafe-model-fidelity>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-cervera-levin-mafe-morphometric-validation>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-cervera-levin-mafe-overall>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-cervera-levin-mafe-parameter-expressivity>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-cervera-levin-mafe-repro-package>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-cervera-levin-mafe-source-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-cervera-levin-mafe-specimen-match> ;
    pk:weightOfEvidence 4.49e-01 .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-cervera-levin-mafe-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cervera–Levin–Mafe gap-junction reaction–diffusion and bioelectric synthesis — Code-to-model traceability: 42/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Major sections are clearly separated and the rusty-matter port names upstream files and line ranges, while the dataset documents that its empirical records are annotation rather than calibrated physiology. But the reaction–diffusion equations are not mapped to numbered equations, figures or parameter tables in Cervera 2021, and the full text was unavailable to verify the docstring's claim of implementation. Critical synthesis choices — crop f2 values, wound gains, 0.13 scaling, f2=0.58 boundary, 0.50/0.55 head thresholds and model-time-to-hours conversion — have no source anchor. Comments sometimes overstate what is tested: trace parity checks only initial and final selected values, despite saying it compares all sampled frames. Evidence: 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L201–L207: model attribution is generic, with no equation or parameter-table pointer <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e71ca55/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L201-L207>; 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L368–L382: rusty-matter constants are explicitly mapped to upstream files <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e71ca55/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L368-L382>; 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L625–L671: parity implementation reads all samples but compares only step zero and final selected values <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e71ca55/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L625-L671>; 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L883–L934: crop pairs, effective f2 values, wound-derived index and normalization are uncited synthesis choices <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e71ca55/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L883-L934>; 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L1122–L1167: simulation time is linearly relabelled as 24 h and plotted against empirical timing <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e71ca55/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L1122-L1167>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gpt-5.6-sol> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe-code-traceability> ;
    pk:hasProbability 4.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-cervera-levin-mafe-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cervera–Levin–Mafe gap-junction reaction–diffusion and bioelectric synthesis — Model fidelity to source: 38/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "The accessible 2021 abstract supports two antagonistic morphogens along one axis, an independent morphogen along an orthogonal axis, and pattern changes under partial GJ blockade, which the two solver functions qualitatively represent. The full paper was not accessible, so mutual annihilation, end-source discretization, boundary treatment, numerical constants and the choice to reduce only D2 cannot be credited as the published equations. More seriously, the claimed (f2,f3) morphospace never uses f3, and its phase boundary is manually drawn. The rusty-matter circuit matches its own pinned educational Rust source, but that source explicitly uses normalized teaching states and is not evidence that this is the 2020 paper's ion-channel model; agreement with its synthetic traces validates a port, not planarian biology. Evidence: 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L186–L238: implemented axial two-species diffusion, decay, mutual annihilation and endpoint sources <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e71ca55/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L186-L238>; 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L241–L273: independent orthogonal one-species solver <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e71ca55/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L241-L273>; 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L360–L599: separate five-band normalized circuit added to the reaction-diffusion model <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e71ca55/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L360-L599>; 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L936–L943: f3 grid coordinate is ignored, making every row constant along f3 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e71ca55/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L936-L943>; datasets/planform/README.md L21–L27: repository itself describes both mechanisms as qualitative or semi-quantitative abstractions without calibrated physiology <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e71ca55/datasets/planform/README.md#L21-L27>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gpt-5.6-sol> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:hasProbability 3.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "unfaithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-cervera-levin-mafe-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cervera–Levin–Mafe gap-junction reaction–diffusion and bioelectric synthesis — Morphometric validation: 25/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "The figure includes real PlanformDB outcome frequencies and the CSV reports circuit states and wavefronts, which is more than an unmeasured illustration. However, the model curves are merely overlaid on the empirical bars: no loss, uncertainty, correlation, held-out prediction or parameter fit is computed, and hand-selected crop mappings closely echo the observed gradient. The silhouette IoU compares two decoded cartoons with each other, not either cartoon with a specimen. Finally, each crop CSV wavefront is reconstructed with a 0.26 multiplier after the shift was normalized by 0.13, so, for example, f2=0.92 is reported as 0.5153 although the solver gives 0.5076; the quantitative output therefore does not faithfully report its own simulation. Evidence: 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L842–L859: empirical double-head frequencies are loaded from curated records <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e71ca55/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L842-L859>; 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L894–L934: model-to-crop mappings and percentage normalization are chosen in code, without a fit <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e71ca55/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L894-L934>; 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L970–L993: CSV doubles simulated displacement through 0.50 + 0.26*shift after shift used a 0.13 denominator <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e71ca55/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L970-L993>; 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L1070–L1119: empirical bars and model indices are plotted together without a validation statistic <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e71ca55/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L1070-L1119>; cervera_levin_mafe_metrics.csv (generated output, not in repo): reproducible table, but crop rd_wavefront_x_star values do not equal direct solver wavefronts — cervera_levin_mafe_metrics.csv: rendered output of 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py, not present when the audit was snapshotted (unfingerprinted)." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gpt-5.6-sol> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:hasProbability 2.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "unfaithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-cervera-levin-mafe-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cervera–Levin–Mafe gap-junction reaction–diffusion and bioelectric synthesis — MorphoEval overall 44.9/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "A deterministic synthesis combines a one-dimensional antagonistic reaction–diffusion solver, an orthogonal one-species profile, a Python port of rusty-matter's educational five-band circuit, 14 curated PlanformDB outcome records, and two decoded Planform cartoons. The GIF paints red/blue territories on a photographic silhouette and switches between wild-type and double-head cartoons; the additional outputs are cervera_levin_mafe_bioelectric_morphospace.png and cervera_levin_mafe_metrics.csv. The high-level 2021 premise is recognizable, but equation-level fidelity could not be checked from the inaccessible full paper, the f3 axis has no computational effect, several biological mappings are uncited choices, and the CSV doubles the actual crop wavefront displacement. Overall 44.9/100 (faithfulness 34.8, reproducibility 68.4); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit e71ca55; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0, scipy 1.16.3, scikit-image 0.26.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 38, Morphological realism / specimen match 38, Parameter expressivity 35, Morphometric validation 25, Source and data traceability 78, Code-to-model traceability 42, Reproducibility package 78. Output judged: cervera_levin_mafe_gj_block.gif: rendered output of 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py, not present when the audit was snapshotted (unfingerprinted)." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gpt-5.6-sol> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe> ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Compare generated head/auricle morphometrics with treated specimens or source-paper figures; use the photograph as measurable geometry rather than only a backdrop.",
        "remediation needed: Correct the CSV to write the direct x_star returned by the solver, and add tests that independently recompute every CSV field and fail when either morphospace axis is inert.",
        "remediation needed: Expand trace parity to every sampled value and distinguish numerical port parity from biological validation; test the reaction–diffusion solver and all figure annotations separately.",
        "remediation needed: Implement f3 in the orthogonal model and derive the two-dimensional phenotype rule from the published morphogen-to-shape mapping; otherwise remove the f3 axis and phase-boundary claim.",
        "remediation needed: Obtain the full 2021 paper and map every reaction term, boundary condition, parameter and blocker factor to its equation, table or figure; label the implementation a qualitative analogue if those cannot be matched.",
        "remediation needed: Replace the hand-set crop f2 values, wound gains, time conversion and 0.50/0.55/0.58 thresholds with source-derived or fitted values, documenting training versus held-out records." ;
    pk:hasProbability 4.49e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-cervera-levin-mafe-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cervera–Levin–Mafe gap-junction reaction–diffusion and bioelectric synthesis — Parameter expressivity: 35/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Lowering f2 produces a visible, monotonic wavefront displacement in the plotted range, and the GIF's circuit readout rises enough to trigger a distinct cartoon. The second advertised morphospace parameter f3 has exactly no effect because its loop variable is unused. Crop-specific f2 values and wound gains are fixed lookup tables rather than exposed, independently swept parameters, and the anatomical output is binary at an unsupported 0.55 threshold. Therefore only one of the nominal two reaction–diffusion dimensions demonstrates the criterion. Evidence: 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L862–L870: f2 sweep drives the axial wavefront <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e71ca55/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L862-L870>; 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L894–L934: crop f2 values and normalization scale are hand-set mappings <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e71ca55/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L894-L934>; 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L936–L943: f3 values are generated but never passed to any solver <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e71ca55/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L936-L943>; 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L1288–L1297: GIF jointly maps f2 onto D2 and custom circuit gap scale <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e71ca55/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L1288-L1297>; docs/media/cervera_levin_mafe_gj_block.gif (generated output, not in repo): f2 visibly shifts the boundary, but form changes only by a thresholded cartoon swap — docs/media/cervera_levin_mafe_gj_block.gif: rendered output of 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py, not present when the audit was snapshotted (unfingerprinted)." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gpt-5.6-sol> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:hasProbability 3.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "unfaithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-cervera-levin-mafe-repro-package> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cervera–Levin–Mafe gap-junction reaction–diffusion and bioelectric synthesis — Reproducibility package: 78/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "The requested environment exactly matched Python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0, scipy 1.16.3 and scikit-image 0.26.0; the scientific dependencies are pinned in the lock file. The prescribed self-test, PNG/CSV run and GIF run all completed headlessly. A second run produced byte-identical PNG, CSV and GIF, and the cached photograph and fixtures are hash checked. The score is not higher because the self-test's advertised \"exact\" parity actually allows 0.035 absolute error (observed maximum 0.02625), checks only selected endpoints rather than every sampled trace value, and does not test RD invariants, f3 sensitivity, phenotype thresholds, CSV correctness or plot labels. Evidence: requirements.lock.txt L18–L41: tested numpy, matplotlib, Pillow, scipy and scikit-image versions are pinned <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e71ca55/requirements.lock.txt#L18-L41>; 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L607–L622: fixture digest verification <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e71ca55/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L607-L622>; 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L625–L671: trace test uses tolerance 0.035 and selected initial/final comparisons <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e71ca55/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L625-L671>; 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L1362–L1409: headless-capable CLI for self-test, PNG/CSV and GIF <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e71ca55/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L1362-L1409>; cervera_levin_mafe_bioelectric_morphospace.png (generated output, not in repo): regenerated byte-identically on two runs — cervera_levin_mafe_bioelectric_morphospace.png: rendered output of 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py, not present when the audit was snapshotted (unfingerprinted); cervera_levin_mafe_metrics.csv (generated output, not in repo): regenerated byte-identically on two runs — cervera_levin_mafe_metrics.csv: rendered output of 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py, not present when the audit was snapshotted (unfingerprinted)." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gpt-5.6-sol> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe-repro-package> ;
    pk:hasProbability 7.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-cervera-levin-mafe-source-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cervera–Levin–Mafe gap-junction reaction–diffusion and bioelectric synthesis — Source and data traceability: 78/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "The primary and companion papers, Planform, Oviedo and Durant sources have resolvable DOIs; the external code is pinned to a full commit; all three fixtures and the photograph have SHA-256 pins; and the Planform-derived records retain experiment IDs, sample sizes and database provenance. The rusty-matter commit and fixture paths were independently fetched and checked. The score is limited because the cited 2021 PMID is wrong (the script says 34418508; PubMed resolves the article as 34411690), the full model papers were inaccessible, and the curated fixture is not the raw PlanformDB database, so its transcription was not independently re-derived here. Evidence: 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L6–L44: paper DOIs, external repository commit and photograph provenance; 2021 PMID is incorrect <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e71ca55/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L6-L44>; 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L71–L103: fixture and photograph SHA-256 values plus source URL and credit <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e71ca55/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L71-L103>; datasets/planform/README.md L1–L19: PlanformDB pin, notice, upstream commit, fixture hashes and experiment groups <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e71ca55/datasets/planform/README.md#L1-L19>; datasets/planform/rusty_matter_planformdb_derived_v0.json L1–L39: database identity, raw checksum, citations and explicit selection policy <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e71ca55/datasets/planform/rusty_matter_planformdb_derived_v0.json#L1-L39>; datasets/planform/paper_citations.bib L29–L80: bibliographic entries for the principal model and empirical papers <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e71ca55/datasets/planform/paper_citations.bib#L29-L80>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gpt-5.6-sol> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe-source-traceability> ;
    pk:hasProbability 7.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-cervera-levin-mafe-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cervera–Levin–Mafe gap-junction reaction–diffusion and bioelectric synthesis — Morphological realism / specimen match: 38/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "The territory panel has the recognizable outline of a real Schmidtea mediterranea and the wild-type versus double-head cartoons are visibly distinct in posterior colour and organs. Neither is a generated specimen: the photograph supplies only a binary mask, the morphogens are painted onto it, and a hard readout threshold chooses one of two pre-existing Planform cartoons. No treated or double-head specimen, nor a source-paper morphology panel, is shown side by side. The synthesis PNG also has overlapping panel titles and legends, reducing interpretability, while the GIF's only anatomical change is the categorical cartoon switch. Evidence: 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L124–L180: photograph is segmented to a mask and used only as the canvas for territory colours <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e71ca55/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L124-L180>; 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L699–L771: wild-type and double-head forms are fixed Planform graph cartoons <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e71ca55/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L699-L771>; 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L1336–L1346: uncited 0.55 threshold selects one of the two cartoons <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e71ca55/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L1336-L1346>; docs/media/cervera_levin_mafe_gj_block.gif (generated output, not in repo): distinct categorical cartoons and coloured silhouette, but no simulated anatomical deformation — docs/media/cervera_levin_mafe_gj_block.gif: rendered output of 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py, not present when the audit was snapshotted (unfingerprinted); cervera_levin_mafe_bioelectric_morphospace.png (generated output, not in repo): six-panel output; top-row titles overlap and no specimen comparison is present — cervera_levin_mafe_bioelectric_morphospace.png: rendered output of 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py, not present when the audit was snapshotted (unfingerprinted)." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gpt-5.6-sol> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe-specimen-match> ;
    pk:hasProbability 3.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "unfaithful" .

